// `src/api/` — the public surface. PLACEHOLDER, except for the one thing that
// exists from the first day: the library's single public error identity.
//
// FILLED BY cycle 0.10, governed by `meta/specs/API.md`. `Regex`, `Cache`,
// `Match`, `Captures`, the match iterators and template replacement. A `Match`
// carries byte offsets and never a slice (RX-050, A-2), because a borrow
// cannot travel up the call stack (D-004) — `probe06a_offsets_returned.npk`.
//
// LAYERING (`BUILD.md` §6, rule B-16). May import: `engine`, `compile`,
// `hir`, `syntax`, `unicode`, `core`. NOTHING IN `src/` MAY IMPORT `api` —
// it is the top of the diagram. `src/lib.npk` is the umbrella and sits above
// it, outside the diagram, re-exporting and never being imported.
mod:api;

// THE WHOLE ERROR BUDGET, DECLARED (RX-060, `SAFETY.md` §4 rule S-8).
//
// REACH-002 makes every `error:` that can reach a `failsafe` a MANDATORY named
// arm in every consuming program, and `(*)` does not discharge it. So the
// count of these declarations is the cost of importing this library, it is
// ONE, and a second is a MAJOR version because it is a compiler-enforced
// source break in every consumer.
//
// It is declared here rather than in `src/lib.npk` because `regex_compile` is
// what raises it and `regex_compile` is `api`'s. An identity declared in the
// umbrella would make `api` import `lib` to raise it — an upward edge and a
// cycle through the one file that is supposed to depend on everything and be
// depended on by nothing. `lib.npk` re-exports it instead.
//
// The detail rides in a `PatternError` value with a closed kind enum (S-9):
// thirty ways for a pattern to be malformed, one identity, because a shutdown
// handler does not care which syntax error it was.
pub error:ERegexPattern;
